lisa-design:
- Spec change (coordinator, mid-task): NO floating major tag. Callers pin `@<release commit sha> # vX.Y.Z`; self-release.yml only runs release-please. Do not reintroduce a v<major>-moving job.
- First release 1.0.0 via package-level `initial-version: "1.0.0"` + manifest seeded `{".": "0.0.0"}` (release-please treats 0.0.0 as "no release" and uses initial-version; verified in release-please src manifest.ts/base.ts). Chosen over `release-as` because it needs no follow-up removal. Top-level keys stay equal to release-please/defaults.json so the drift check is quiet; `bootstrap-sha` = a13947d (last legacy commit) so the 1.0.0 changelog starts at #3.
- Manifest: new kind `workflows` (not `action`): at most one, release: false, no depends_on, nobody depends on it. Stages() now only orders release: true repos; Validate still cycle-checks all repos. Renovate and vuln-summary default selection skip kind workflows (named explicitly still works) so mock runs don't touch the workflows repo.
- ccf-bump workflowRef: YAML-per-job scan (jobs.<id>.uses), line-local edits. Target = WorkflowsPin(sha, tag) = "<sha> # vX.Y.Z"; SHA from TagCommit (GET commits/{tag}, peels annotated tags). Sync mode resolves the latest final of the manifest's kind-workflows repo; train mode only with --set. A non-release --set ref is used as given (old behaviour).
- Pin rules: same sha -> comment fix (auto-merge); older same-major sha#ver or tag -> move (auto-merge); main or SHA w/o comment -> move, needs human (Major); other major (older or newer) -> CONFLICT (not moved: v2 may change inputs, and sync would otherwise force-push over a human's migration branch); newer same major -> conflict (never downgrade); other branch/short sha -> conflict.
- workflows-ref: DELETED (not rewritten) with its head comment and an emptied with:, only when the job's pin moves; flow-style with: is an error for a human. notify-failure default changed v1 -> "" and checks out `inputs.workflows-ref || job.workflow_sha`.
- release-checks.yml gets additive input module-path (default true); workflows' ci.yml passes false, since a v2 must not require a /v2 module rename.
